  "datasheet": "https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/bcm2711/bcm2711-peripherals.pdf",
  "verified": true,
  "summary": "The 40-pin GPIO header shared by Raspberry Pi 2B, 3B, 3B+, 4B, Zero and Zero 2 W. 26 GPIOs at 3.3 V, plus 5 V, 3.3 V and ground pins. Pin numbers in code are BCM GPIO numbers.",
  "warnings": [
    {
      "level": "danger",
      "text": "All GPIOs are 3.3 V only and are not 5 V tolerant. Pins 2 and 4 carry 5 V: never connect them to a GPIO.",
      "pins": [
        "pin2",
        "pin4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "text": "Raspberry Pi 5 gets its external I/O from the RP1 south-bridge chip, not the BCM SoC, so its GPIO alternate functions differ from the BCM2835/BCM2711 ones listed here. Do not use this table for a Pi 5."
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "text": "GPIO0/GPIO1 (pins 27/28, ID_SD/ID_SC) are reserved for the HAT ID EEPROM and are probed at boot. Do not use them for anything else.",
      "pins": [
        "pin27",
        "pin28"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "Functions marked [Pi 4B only] appear only in the BCM2711 table: extra UARTs 2-5, I2C 3-6, SPI 3-6, the SD0 interface and the DPI/LCD signals (the BCM2835 table marks ALT2 as reserved on these pins). Functions marked [Pi 2/3/Zero only] appear only in the BCM2835 table: the BSC/SPI slave on GPIO18-21 (moved to GPIO8-11 on the BCM2711) and ARM JTAG on ALT5 of GPIO4/5/6/12/13. Only one function per pin can be active at a time."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "Hardware PWM is on GPIO12, GPIO13, GPIO18 and GPIO19. Software PWM works on any GPIO. UART1 (TXD1/RXD1) is the mini UART. \"SMI\" functions are the BCM Secondary Memory Interface."
    }
  ],
